# Images belonging to posts. Same rule as content/ below: this is the author's
# material, not the project's source. They are uploaded through /admin, which
# stores them in the data volume under data/images/ and serves them from
# /images/ — nothing needs them in the repo, and a post's artwork would
# otherwise put megabytes of binaries into git history permanently.
#
# Site chrome that IS source (a default OG image, say) can be committed with
# `git add -f`, or lives beside the other static assets outside this directory.
/static/images/

# The author's content, not the project's source.
#
# Posts and site.yml are data. They are written by hand, by /admin, by the REST
# API, and by MCP tools — the admin and API paths rewrite site.yml through a
# YAML round trip, so tracking it here would mean every edit made on a running
# site shows up as a diff and every deploy risks a conflict against it.
#
# This is not backed up by being in the repo. Back up content/ and data/
# together as part of the deployment's backup routine.
/content/

# Working notes: deployment runbooks, design specs, and implementation plans.
# They track the author's machine rather than the source, so they stay local
# and out of the history.
/docs/

# Generated
/public/
/data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Build output
/dist/
/dtcom
/dtcom.exe

# Editor / OS
*.swp
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Env
.env
